The '''2009 FIFA Club World Cup final''' was the final match of the [[2009 FIFA Club World Cup]], a [[association football|football]] tournament for the champion clubs from each of [[FIFA]]'s six continental confederations. The match took place at the [[Zayed Sports City Stadium|Sheikh Zayed Stadium]], [[Abu Dhabi]], on 19 December 2009, and pitted [[Estudiantes de La Plata]] of Argentina, the [[CONMEBOL]] club champions, against [[FC Barcelona|Barcelona]] of Spain, the [[UEFA]] club champions.

Estudiantes forward [[Mauro Boselli]] opened the scoring in the 37th minute, but [[Pedro (footballer, born 1987)|Pedro]] equalised for Barcelona with one minute left in regulation time. [[Lionel Messi]] scored the winning goal in the fifth minute of the second half of extra time, securing Barcelona's record sixth trophy for the 2009 calendar year.<ref>{{cite news |title=Barcelona beat Estudiantes to win the Club World Cup |url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/8422908.stm |work=BBC Sport |publisher=BBC |date=19 December 2009 |access-date=21 December 2009 }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Messi seals number six |url=http://soccernet.espn.go.com/report?id=285375&league=FIFA.CWC&cc=5739 |work=ESPN Soccernet |date=19 December 2009 |access-date=21 December 2009 |archive-date=20 October 2012 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121020091844/http://soccernet.espn.go.com/report?id=285375&league=FIFA.CWC&cc=5739 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

